    "notes": "Hermitage Bridge has the low single granite vault, curved parapets, rounded ends, broad roadway, both walks and the three mapped short stair reaches. Water stage, embankment grade and carved stonework are visualization approximations. The viewer’s procedural sidewalk contributes an overlapping raised edge at two off-center sample points, up to 37.2 cm above the matched approach grade. The separate museum crossing and surrounding buildings retain native geometry."
